// EXPECT-DIAG: E076
// EXPECT-DIAG: not representable in type 'int'
// OVH-014 (docs/planning/OVERHAUL_REMAINING_WORK.md), FREEZE.md §6.2 row 6:
// "Compile-time on typed constants: error." Before this fix, referencing an
// `immut int` local inside further literal arithmetic was NOT folded --
// `tryFoldUntypedIntConstant()` had no case for `VariableExprAST` -- so this
// compiled successfully and only trapped at RUNTIME (via the ordinary
// checked-arithmetic path), even though `a` is a compile-time-known typed
// constant, not a runtime value. Contrast with fail_runtime_overflow_add.tr
// in this same folder, where the operand truly is a `mut` (a real runtime
// value) -- that one is correctly a runtime trap; this one must now be a
// COMPILE-time E076, exactly like fail_compile_time_literal_arithmetic_
// overflow.tr's bare-literal case, since `a + 1` folds to the same
// out-of-range value once `a`'s own known-exact value is substituted in.
fn main(): int {
    immut a: int = 9223372036854775807;
    immut b = a + 1;
    return b to int;
}
